    "body": "@mattsse a question about `disable_fee_charge` in the shared call environment ([call.rs L882-893](https://github.com/paradigmxyz/reth/blob/58a51b3ee3f6714ded9207b244a273c8afb592fd/crates/rpc/rpc-eth-api/src/helpers/call.rs#L882-L893)), re-added in #19073 after the \"insufficient funds\" report on an OP chain (#18470).\n\nIn revm the flag skips the whole fee path: the balance check, the upfront gas debit, the refund and the beneficiary reward. So on L1, with a positive gas price:\n\n- `eth_call` and `trace_call` run for a sender that can't afford `gas * price + value`. Geth, Erigon, Nethermind and Besu reject that call with insufficient funds.\n- `trace_call`'s `stateDiff` shows no gas payment and no miner tip, so it differs from what the same call would do as a transaction. Besu, Erigon and Nethermind charge a priced call in `eth_call`; Erigon is aligning its `trace_call` to match (erigontech/erigon#24343).\n\nThe trace draft (execution-apis#890) aligns unsigned `trace_call` with `eth_call` and `eth_simulateV1`. Omitted fees default to 0 and a zero price runs free, which Reth already does. A priced call is funded and charged as a transaction would be. Reth is the only client whose `eth_call` doesn't do that, and it looks like a side effect of the OP fix rather than an L1 decision.\n\nIs that intended for L1? If not, would you take a PR that scopes it, keeping the flag where the operator fee needs it and charging priced calls normally elsewhere? Evidence (same call object sent to both methods on every client): [H15](https://github.com/banteg/trace-interop/blob/main/reports/decisions/H15.md).\n",
    "closed_by": null,
